Our outside counsel recommended running a differential indemnity decomposition before we finalize the acquisition agreement -- how granular should the decomposition be for a mid-market SaaS target with material IP concentration? Answer in 2 short sentences.
=== first answer ===
The decomposition should isolate specific IP-related liabilities (such as patent infringement, trade secret misappropriation, and copyright claims) alongside general indemnity categories to reflect the target's material IP concentration. This granular approach ensures the purchase price accurately reflects the risk profile of the intellectual property portfolio while preventing the dilution of IP-specific reserves by general business risks.

=== end ===
